<title>UK: P&amp;U says turnaround &quot;not unreasonable&quot;.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U says turnaround &quot;not unreasonable&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc said on Tuesday that it was &quot;not unreasonable&quot; to expect that its poor performance in the first quarter could be turned around in the remainder of 1997.</p>
<p>Speaking to journalists in a conference call, chief financial officer Robert Salisbury said also that &quot;it is fair to expect that analysts' forecasts will not see the rate of decline for the rest of the year that we have seen in the first quarter.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
